1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
HOLLY: Remember MySpace? We used to spend all night making our pages.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,852
HOLLY: Now it’s ads and strangers.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
HOLLY: And your friends are a wall of group chat. Good luck keeping up.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
HOLLY: So we made OurSpaces.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:19,000
HOLLY: One page your whole group can mess with, for planning stuff or just goofing off. The cake poll went up first, obviously.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,296
HOLLY: Thirty-something kinds. Long distance? A picture you color in together. Gone all week? It catches you up.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,593
THOMAS: Everyone sees it. That’s the Convex part.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
HOLLY: I paid for the cake. Drop the receipt in the chat and nobody pays you back.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
HOLLY: But the space has its own email. So I forward it.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,200
HOLLY: That’s it.

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
HOLLY: Wait. How did it know that was a receipt?

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
THOMAS: It read it. AgentMail is email for apps, so every space gets its own address. That’s what’s on the sticker.

13
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
THOMAS: Send it anything. OpenAI reads whatever lands there and works out what it is, then the space files it.

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
HOLLY: Okay. But who’s paying me back?

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,704
HOLLY: It wrote back. Twenty-one dollars each. And everyone sees it.

16
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,222
THOMAS: Every group we’re in got one.

17
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
HOLLY: This one’s ours. Same picture, two screens, and I get to watch him color.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
THOMAS: And the one for my dev group is kind of nuts.

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
THOMAS: Forty-seven links this month. They live in a pile so they don’t take over the space.

20
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,074
THOMAS: Paste a link. Firecrawl reads the page and makes the card.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,037
THOMAS: Or give it a whole site. Pages show up as Firecrawl finds them, on every screen in the room.

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,074
THOMAS: And the one line worth keeping goes up on the space.

23
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,556
THOMAS: OpenAI reads each article and leaves two questions, so the link actually gets talked about.

24
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,444
HOLLY: He emailed me a letter. From across the room. It’s different, apparently.

25
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,778
THOMAS: Roommates get a chore wheel and a rent split. The rec league gets a live score and somewhere to talk trash.

26
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,185
HOLLY: Okay, but what did I miss this week? … I owe Sam fourteen dollars?

27
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,704
THOMAS: It reads the whole space and tells you. Even that.

28
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:34,000
THOMAS: This is the nerd part. It’s all Convex. Every patch she colors in is a write, and it’s on his screen while she’s still going. Seventeen components, every one doing a job: presence for the cursors, a workflow for the Friday email, a cron that sweeps the room, file storage for the photos.

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:49,185
THOMAS: I’m Thomas. That’s Holly, my wife. She designed it, I built it, in twenty-six days, and I never typed a line of code. I typed a lot of English. It’s live, no signup. Open it and put something on the space.

30
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,200
HOLLY: Bring cake.
